1.1.text:
CHAPTER IV
FORMS OF VIOLENCE
Article 5
(1) Forms of Gender-Based Violence include a. Physical Violence;
b. Psychological Violence;
c. Sexual Violence;
(2) Forms of Violence against Children include a. Physical Violence;
b. Psychological Violence;
c. Sexual Violence;
d. Neglect;
e. Exploitation;
f. Maltreatment

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
The protection of victims of gender-based violence and children is based on Pancasila and grounded in the 1945 Constitution, as well as basic principles that include:
a. non-discrimination;
b. the best interests of victims;
c. gender justice and equality;
d. victim protection;
e. maternal survival;
f. child survival, growth, and development;
g. respect for the child's opinion;
h. transparency;
i. integration;
j. not blaming the victim;
k. empowering;
l. victim confidentiality;
m. decision-making in the hands of the victim.

CHAPTER V
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 12
Every victim of gender-based violence and children shall receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity respected as a human being;
b. the right to determine their own decisions;
c. the right to obtain information;
d. the right to confidentiality of their identity;
e. the right to complaint handling;
f. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
g. the right to obtain facilitation in the judicial process;
h. the right to obtain repatriation efforts and social reintegration of victims of gender-based violence and children.
i. the right to social rehabilitation.

CHAPTER III
OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Article 4
(1) The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to implement efforts to prevent the occurrence of violence in the form of:
a. providing data and information regarding gender and child victims of violence in accordance with laws and regulations;
b. conducting education on anti-violence values based on gender and violence against children; and
c. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and child victims of violence.
jdih.pekalongankab.go.id (2) To anticipate the occurrence of acts of violence, the Regional Government has the obligation to provide and organize services for victims in the form of:
a. establishing and facilitating the operation of integrated service institutions for victims by involving elements of SKPD, Agencies, Institutions, Community Organizations, Communities;
b. providing facilities and infrastructure;
c. increasing the capacity of service provider institutions;
d. conducting coordination and cooperation in the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based violence and children;
e. conducting monitoring and evaluation.
f. encouraging public awareness of the importance of protection for victims.
(3) The Regional Government in carrying out obligations as referred to in paragraph (1) and (2) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands or other persons who are legally responsible for the victim.

REGENT OF PEKALONGAN,

Considering : a. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity, honor and worth, and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence and discrimination as a form of respect, protection and enforcement of Human Rights, particularly the basic rights of women and children, so it is necessary to regulate the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based violence and children in Pekalongan Regency;
b. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation of Pekalongan Regency concerning the Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Children;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 13 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions within the Province of Central Java;
3. Law Number 9 of 1965 concerning the Establishment of Second Level Region of Batang by amending Law Number 13 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions within the Province of Central Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1965 Number 52, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2757);
4. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);
5. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);
jdih.pekalongankab.go.id
6. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
7. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
8. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4437), as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 12 of 2008 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4844);
9. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);
10. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
11. Government Regulation Number 48 of 1986 concerning the Transfer of the Capital of Second Level Regency of Pekalongan from the Territory of Second Level Municipality of Pekalongan to Kajen City in the Territory of Second Level Regency of Pekalongan (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1986 Number 70);
12. Government Regulation Number 21 of 1988 concerning Changes to the Territorial Boundaries of Second Level Municipality of Pekalongan, Second Level Regency of Pekalongan and Second Level Regency of Batang (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1988 Number 42, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3381);
13. Government Regulation Number 79 of 2005 concerning Guidance and Supervision of Regional Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2005 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4593);
14. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);
jdih.pekalongankab.go.id
15. Government Regulation Number 9 of 2008 concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of Criminal Acts of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818);
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards (SPM) in the Field of Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2010 Number 56);
17. Regional Regulation of Pekalongan Regency Number 8 of 2008 concerning Government Affairs That Are the Authority of Regional Government (Regional Gazette of Pekalongan Regency Year 2008 Number 8);
18. Regional Regulation of Pekalongan Regency Number 6 of 2011 concerning Organization and Work Procedures of Regional Technical Institutions, Civil Service Police Unit and Regional Disaster Management Agency (Regional Gazette of Pekalongan Regency Year 2011 Number 6, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Pekalongan Regency Number 22);

With Mutual Approval

